  "uuid": "9435a1e0-f7fd-401f-894d-8fb1075a5d3c",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "c79a1296-edbf-1b5e-a69e-4c2b29b480ff",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "9ec00f4c-b802-ef8c-d4a9-80c76a3c8b1b",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Being mindful of the two key deficiencies in the provincial education system - access to educational opportunities and low quality of education- the plan provides the provincial government an opportunity to take systematic steps to ensure equity in access, enhance the quality, improve governance and service delivery, and facilitate equity in resource allocation. Developed on the basis of the fundamental tenets of the National Education Policy and the National Curriculum, SESP is envisioned to contribute towards achieving the National Poverty Reduction Strategy goals, the internationally-agreed Education for All commitments, Millennium Development Goals and, most importantly, the recently passed Sindh Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education Act, 2013.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The plan has been developed after two years of extensive consultation and engagement of key stakeholders from the public and private education sectors in Sindh. IED played a key role in developing the Plan's vision and strategy with faculty being part of two consultative groups during the two years. Professor Dr Muhammad Memon, as part of the Expert Advisory Group provided input on the long-term policy objectives and strategic direction of the plan, while Dr Sajid Ali, Assistant Professor, was part of the Local Education Group, which worked as a broader consultative body for developing the details of the plan. They were building on IED's experience with the development of the National Education Policy in 2009 and review of the National Curriculum Framework in 2006.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
