    },
    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Efforts to reform education in Sindh received a boost with the launch of the Sindh Education Sector Plan (SESP) 2014-18 by the provincial government on September 29, 2014. This Rs. 940bn plan aims to educate children aged five to 16 in Sindh and is supported by donors including the European Union, Global Partnership in Education, USAID and the World Bank. The formulation of SESP represents an important policy and planning milestone in the ongoing education reform process in Sindh following the 18th Amendment to the Constitution of the country which devolved the responsibility of providing free and compulsory education to all children aged five to 16 years to the provincial governments.",
